atlas identity

architecture actor-graph
  canonical_name ActorGraph
  owns Actor
  owns Relation
  consumes Corroboration
  consumes Occurrence
  consumes CommunicationEvent
  publishes Actor
  publishes Relation
  family identity
  domain Identity / Institutional Capacity
  layer identity
  semantic_question Who is this real-world actor, and for which profile is that identity verified?
  purpose Real actors with identifier assertions, observations, corroboration, and per-profile verification. The verified-for law is the point.
  maturity implemented
  node_types Actor
  node_types IdentifierAssertion
  node_types Corroboration
  node_types VerificationProfile
  edge_types asserts
  edge_types corroborates
  edge_types affiliated_with
  state_types asserted
  state_types observed
  state_types corroborated
  state_types verified_for
  state_types contradicted
  invariant asserted_via_email is not verified_for(ACM.editor)
  forbidden_inference email sender -> verified institutional role
  forbidden_inference affiliation -> authority
  forbidden_inference identity similarity -> same actor
  invariant provenance is mandatory on every actor and edge; confidence tier {verified,asserted,inferred} never collapses (native + python parity on the shared actor_nodes/actor_edges store)
  native_format graf
  command BonfyreEntity
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/actors.py
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/pack_loader.py
  source_path engine/core/src/actor.c
  source_path engine/core/include/bf_actor.h
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_actors.py
  witness engine/core/tests/actor_graph_test.c
  source_lineage capitalgym crm relationships
  known_gap native writer records actors/edges on the shared store with the declared-kind, mandatory-provenance and non-collapsing-confidence gates (python reads native-written rows, tier preserved -- proven); native corroboration/verification-profile promotion logic is the remaining native-absorption item

architecture verification-ledger
  canonical_name VerificationLedger
  owns Corroboration
  consumes Actor
  consumes FortificationPlan
  publishes Corroboration
  publishes Actor
  family identity
  domain Identity / Institutional Capacity
  layer identity
  semantic_question Is this actor independently corroborated enough to promote asserted -> verified?
  purpose The gated mechanism a fortification "verify" action executes against. Records corroborations (actor, source, evidence) and promotes asserted -> verified only at a threshold of INDEPENDENT sources, never on the actor's own say-so. Closes the feedback loop: a load-bearing asserted actor is a fortification target; once independently corroborated and promoted, it drops off the CollapseFront verify plan -- risk actually retired, not merely noted.
  maturity measured
  node_types Corroboration
  edge_types corroborates
  state_types asserted
  state_types verified
  internal_calculus distinct-source count gate; monotone promotion at threshold k (default 2)
  invariant independence is by distinct source; a repeated source is one corroboration, so an actor cannot bootstrap its own verification
  invariant promotion is monotone -- never demotes, never promotes below threshold
  invariant promotion writes back through actors.upsert_actor, so the confidence change is a normal graph write, not a side channel
  forbidden_inference a corroboration was recorded -> the actor is verified (below threshold it stays asserted)
  forbidden_inference promoted to verified -> the claim is true (independently attested is not proven)
  interacts actor-graph
  interacts collapse-front
  interacts fortification-plan
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/verification.py
  source_path engine/core/src/corroboration.c
  source_path engine/core/include/bf_corroboration.h
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_verification.py
  witness engine/core/tests/corroboration_test.c
  source_lineage fortification verify action needs a real gated mechanism
  known_gap native ledger records corroborations on the shared actor_corroborations store with distinct-source independence (python reads native-written rows -- parity proven); the promotion gate stays python/human (native never promotes -- the human line)

architecture hash-identity
  canonical_name HashIdentityGraph
  family identity
  domain Identity
  layer identity
  semantic_question Are these byte/content objects identical?
  purpose Content-addressed identity: bytes -> digest -> Merkle membership. Used by artifacts, packs, model weights, receipts.
  maturity implemented
  node_types ContentObject
  edge_types hashes_to
  edge_types merkle_member_of
  forbidden_inference same bytes -> same derivational meaning
  native_format graf
  command BonfyreHash
  source_path cmd/BonfyreHash
  source_lineage identity federation seed
